    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Emperor Sigismund made Savoy a duchy in 1416, joining French-speaking Alpine lands with Italian-speaking Piedmont.</li><li>Restored in 1559 after French occupation, it moved its capital to Turin and became a disciplined absolutist military state.</li><li>Its dukes became kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sicily">Sicily</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sardinia">Sardinia</a>, and their kingdom later united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#italy">Italy</a>; Savoy itself passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a> in 1860.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Amadeus VIII, the first Duke of Savoy, retired to a lakeside priory and was then elected antipope as Felix V by the Council of Basel in 1439.</p></aside>
    </section>

